  "chain": "battery cell terminal cracking (cell 21, intergranular SCC) [provisional cause] -> battery #2 voltage fluctuations -> control power fluctuations on shared ESS buses -> Unit 1 RFP trips -> automatic Unit 1 scram -> Unit 1 shutdown [backups RCIC, ADS, EDG]; separately -> ESS Bus 14-1 trip / ATS transfer to non-safety power -> TS-required equipment inoperable (Buses 14-1, 23-1)",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two parallel failure chains present: (1) battery cell cracking -> voltage fluctuation -> RFP trips -> scram; (2) same voltage fluctuation -> bus 14-1 trip / ATS transfer -> TS inoperability of buses 14-1 and 23-1. A third, independent failure mode (inadequate RFP feed breaker auxiliary contact closure, installed at refuel outage) caused the 3rd RFP's failure to trip automatically and a separate ~46-day LCO 3.3.2.2 violation; this is modeled as its own origin (no CAUSED_BY to the official cause node, since official cause code TBD/provisional applies to the battery failure per Block 13 EJ/BTRY). HPCI is not mentioned in this narrative (RCIC/ADS/EDG serve as backups instead). System Design paragraph on DC power system architecture treated as design context, not modeled as extra nodes beyond EJ. Cause code is TBD/provisional per Block 13's cause field '!IIJ' which does not map to a standard single-letter code; category left as 'provisional' per form."
}